.SS "void p8est_balance (\fBp8est_t\fP * p8est, \fBp8est_connect_type_t\fP btype, \fBp8est_init_t\fP init_fn)"

.PP
2:1 balance the size differences of neighboring elements in a forest\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp8est\fP\fP The \fBp8est\fP to be worked on\&. 
.br
\fIbtype\fP Balance type (face, edge, or corner/full)\&. Examples: Finite volume or discontinuous Galerkin methods only require face balance\&. Continuous finite element methods usually require edge balance\&. Corner balance is almost never required mathematically; it just produces a smoother mesh grading\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data which is already allocated automatically\&. 
.RE
.PP

