.SS "\fBp8est_t\fP* p8est_copy (\fBp8est_t\fP * input, int copy_data)"

.PP
Make a deep copy of a \fBp8est\fP\&. The connectivity is not duplicated\&. Copying of quadrant user data is optional\&. If old and new data sizes are 0, the user_data field is copied regardless\&. The inspect member of the copy is set to NULL\&. The revision counter of the copy is set to zero\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIcopy_data\fP If true, data are copied\&. If false, data_size is set to 0\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns a valid \fBp8est\fP that does not depend on the input, except for borrowing the same connectivity\&. Its revision counter is 0\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_destroy (\fBp8est_t\fP * p8est)"

.PP
Destroy a \fBp8est\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The connectivity structure is not destroyed with the \fBp8est\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBExamples\fP
.in +1c
\fBsimple/simple3\&.c\fP\&.
.SS "\fBp8est_t\fP* p8est_load (const char * filename, sc_MPI_Comm mpicomm, size_t data_size, int load_data, void * user_pointer, \fBp8est_connectivity_t\fP ** connectivity)"

.PP
Load the complete connectivity/p8est structure from disk\&. This is a collective operation that all MPI processes need to call\&. All processes read from the same file, so the filename given needs to be identical over all parallel invocations\&.
.PP
By default, a file can only be loaded with the same number of processors that it was stored with\&. The defaults can be changed with \fBp8est_load_ext()\fP in \fBp8est_extended\&.h\fP\&.
.PP
The revision counter of the loaded \fBp4est\fP is set to zero\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfilename\fP Name of the file to read\&. 
.br
\fImpicomm\fP A valid MPI communicator\&. 
.br
\fIdata_size\fP Size of data for each quadrant which can be zero\&. Then user_data_pool is set to NULL\&. If data_size is zero, load_data is ignored\&. 
.br
\fIload_data\fP If true, the element data is loaded\&. This is only permitted if the saved data size matches\&. If false, the stored data size is ignored\&. 
.br
\fIuser_pointer\fP Assign to the user_pointer member of the \fBp8est\fP before init_fn is called the first time\&. 
.br
\fIconnectivity\fP Connectivity must be destroyed separately\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Returns a valid forest structure\&. A pointer to a valid connectivity structure is returned through the last argument\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Aborts on file errors or invalid file contents\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "size_t p8est_memory_used (\fBp8est_t\fP * p8est)"

.PP
Calculate local memory usage of a forest structure\&. Not collective\&. The memory used on the current rank is returned\&. The connectivity structure is not counted since it is not owned; use p8est_connectivity_memory_usage (p8est->connectivity)\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp8est\fP\fP Valid forest structure\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Memory used in bytes\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBp8est_t\fP* p8est_new (sc_MPI_Comm mpicomm, \fBp8est_connectivity_t\fP * connectivity, size_t data_size, \fBp8est_init_t\fP init_fn, void * user_pointer)"

.PP
Create a new forest with an initial coarse mesh\&. The new forest consists of equi-partitioned root quadrants\&. When there are more processors than trees, some processors are empty\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImpicomm\fP A valid MPI communicator\&. 
.br
\fIconnectivity\fP This is the connectivity information that the forest is built with\&. Note the \fBp8est\fP does not take ownership of the memory\&. 
.br
\fIdata_size\fP This is the size of data for each quadrant which can be zero\&. Then user_data_pool is set to NULL\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data which is already allocated automatically\&. 
.br
\fIuser_pointer\fP Assign to the user_pointer member of the \fBp8est\fP before init_fn is called the first time\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This returns a valid forest\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The connectivity structure must not be destroyed during the lifetime of this forest\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void p8est_partition (\fBp8est_t\fP * p8est, int allow_for_coarsening, \fBp8est_weight_t\fP weight_fn)"

.PP
Equally partition the forest\&. The partition can be by element count or by a user-defined weight\&.
.PP
The forest will be partitioned between processors such that they have an approximately equal number of quadrants (or sum of weights)\&.
.PP
The user data of a quadrant is transferred along within this function\&.
.PP
On one process, the function noops and does not call the weight callback\&. Otherwise, the weight callback is called once per quadrant in order\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp8est\fP\fP The forest that will be partitioned\&. 
.br
\fIallow_for_coarsening\fP Slightly modify partition such that quadrant families are not split between ranks\&. 
.br
\fIweight_fn\fP A weighting function or NULL for uniform partitioning\&. When running with mpisize == 1, never called\&. Otherwise, called in order for all quadrants if not NULL\&. A weighting function with constant weight 1 on each quadrant is equivalent to weight_fn == NULL but other constant weightings may result in different uniform partitionings\&. 
.RE
.PP

