.SS "void p8est_reset_data (\fBp8est_t\fP * p8est, size_t data_size, \fBp8est_init_t\fP init_fn, void * user_pointer)"

.PP
Reset user pointer and element data\&. When the data size is changed the quadrant data is freed and allocated\&. The initialization callback is invoked on each quadrant\&. Old user_data content is disregarded\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdata_size\fP This is the size of data for each quadrant which can be zero\&. Then user_data_pool is set to NULL\&. 
.br
\fIinit_fn\fP Callback function to initialize the user_data which is already allocated automatically\&. May be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIuser_pointer\fP Assign to the user_pointer member of the \fBp8est\fP before init_fn is called the first time\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "long p8est_revision (\fBp8est_t\fP * p8est)"

.PP
Return the revision counter of the forest\&. Not collective, even though the revision value is the same on all ranks\&. A newly created forest starts with a revision counter of zero\&. Every refine, coarsen, partition, and balance that actually changes the mesh increases the counter by one\&. Operations with no effect keep the old value\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp8est\fP\fP The forest must be valid\&. 
