.SS "void p8est_save (const char * filename, \fBp8est_t\fP * p8est, int save_data)"

.PP
Save the complete connectivity/p8est data to disk\&. This is a collective operation that all MPI processes need to call\&. All processes write into the same file, so the filename given needs to be identical over all parallel invocations\&.
.PP
By default, we write the current processor count and partition into the file header\&. This makes the file depend on mpisize\&. For changing this see \fBp8est_save_ext()\fP in \fBp8est_extended\&.h\fP\&.
.PP
The revision counter is not saved to the file, since that would make files different that come from different revisions but store the same mesh\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfilename\fP Name of the file to write\&. 
.br
\fI\fBp8est\fP\fP Valid forest structure\&. 
.br
\fIsave_data\fP If true, the element data is saved\&. Otherwise, a data size of 0 is saved\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Aborts on file errors\&. 
.PP
If \fBp4est\fP is not configured to use MPI-IO, some processes return from this function before the file is complete, in which case immediate read-access to the file may require a call to sc_MPI_Barrier\&. 
.RE
.PP

